(O101 - Tool Measure)
(Measures current tool length using the tool setter)
(Requires: [TOOL_SETTER] X, Y, VEL, REF_Z, MAX_PROBE_DEPTH in LinuxCNC INI)
(Stores result in LinuxCNC tool table via G10 L1)

O101 sub

    (Read machine settings from LinuxCNC INI)
    #<setter_x> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]X>
    #<setter_y> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]Y>
    #<setter_vel> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]VEL>
    #<setter_ref_z> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]REF_Z>
    #<max_depth> = #<_ini[TOOL_SETTER]MAX_PROBE_DEPTH>
    #<tool_num> = #<_current_tool>

    (Safety: ensure spindle is off and machine is in a known state)
    M5
    M9
    G90
    G40
    G49

    (Retract Z to safe height, then move to tool setter XY)
    G53 G0 Z0
    G53 G0 X#<setter_x> Y#<setter_y>

    (Fast probe down to find approximate setter surface)
    G91
    G38.2 Z[0 - #<max_depth>] F[#<setter_vel> * 4]
    G0 Z2.0
    G38.2 Z-4.0 F#<setter_vel>
    G90

    (Calculate tool length relative to setter reference)
    #<tool_length> = [#5063 - #<setter_ref_z>]

    (Store in tool table and activate offset)
    G10 L1 P#<tool_num> Z#<tool_length>
    G43 H#<tool_num>

    (Retract to safe height)
    G53 G0 Z0

    (MSG, Tool measure complete. Tool #<tool_num> length: #<tool_length>)

O101 endsub
M2
